//-------------------- Help Texts --------------------
HlpCLIAppName  sample
HlpUsage       "sample [format=\"FORMATSPEC\" [now]|[file FILENAME]"
AppInfo |
    @HL-ALib App Sample V. {}.{}
    (c) 2025-{} AWorx GmbH. Published under MIT License (Open Source).
    For more information, see: https://alib.dev/alib_mod_app.html
    @HL-

HlpGeneral >
  \nABOUT sample\n
  @>>
  This is a sample application provided with C++ library 'ALib' to demonstrate the use of its
  module \"ALib App\"."
  \n@<<

//-------------------- CLI Commands/Options/Parameters/ExitCodes --------------------
DateC<    datesample::Commands::
       // enum       ident          minread     Params
DateC ~|
  1,         now            ,1         ,                 ,     \
  2,         file           ,1         ,filename


THlpCmdSht_now      "Reports the actual date/time"
THlpCmdLng_now
  Reports the actual date/time. May be omitted, as this is the default if no command is given.

THlpCmdSht_file     Returns the date/time of a file.
THlpCmdLng_file     Returns the last modification date/time of a file.

DateO<       datesample::Options::
//enum  ident        minread    identChar   in-arg-separ.   args to consume    ShortcutTo
DateO ~|
  0,    format        ,1,          f,          =               ,1                ,

TOptUsg_format   --format[=]\"placeholders\"
TOptHlp_format  >
    Sets the output format. The format specification is given with the documentation of the
    ALib method CalendarDateTime::Format, found here:\n
    https://alib.dev/classalib_1_1strings_1_1util_1_1CalendarDateTime.html



DateP<  datesample::Parameters::
//enum  name           minIdentLen   identifier    in-arg-sep   delim   args to consume  isOptional
//                                   (if empty -> mandatory!)
DateP ~|
 0,    FILENAME           ,1,                             ,            =    ,    ,-1          ,0

THlpParSht_FILENAME   Mandatory parameter of command \"file\".
THlpParLng_FILENAME=>
  Denotes the file that is used for retrieving the modification date.
  This parameter is mandatory to be given with command 'file' and has to be appended to this
  command, separated by '='"


DateE<  datesample::
//enum  name                            assoc. cli exception
DateE ~|
  101,ErrMissingFilename               ,-1,   
  102,ErrFileNotFound                  ,-1,   
  103,ErrPermissionDenied              ,-1

TExit101   Command 'file' given without a filename argument.
TExit102   File not found.
TExit103   Permission denied.

// custom resources
FNOTFND    The file {!Q} specified with command 'file' was not found.
FNOACC     Access denied to file {!Q} specified with command 'file'.
MSNGFNAME  Error: no filename given with command 'file'.

// DOX_MARKER([DOX_ALIB_SAMPLE_ALIBRC])
